ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: green
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [Lexical bag-cosine recovers only a fraction of latent confusability c — the ~0.2 AUC oracle gap is exactly the "noisy single-factor readout of a latent" prediction from classical measurement-error theory, no emergent phenomenon needed; self-logprob being a joint readout of (c,d) trivially dominates any single-factor proxy by sufficiency — this is textbook (a sufficient statistic for the latent beats a lossier marginal proxy); generic-difficulty predictor winning is expected given bd=1.8 is comparable to bc=2.6 AND d is recovered cleanly while c is recovered poorly (effective signal = beta * recovery-fidelity, and difficulty wins on the second factor); AUC dropping toward 0.5 as K grows is the standard "max-of-K order-statistic of a noisy similarity loses discriminative power as K grows and the max saturates" effect, not a real phase transition.]
CONFOUNDS: [None material to the kill — anti-circular construction held (label from latent c+d, predictor reads schema-only tokens), oracle gap ~0.2 AUC empirically demonstrates the readout is genuinely lossy rather than label-leaking; the kill is INTERNAL to the generative model the claim assumes, so confound risk runs the other way (favoring the claim, not against it).]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [Generative model assumes self-logprob is a readout of BOTH c and d — this is the assumption that makes the "adds beyond logprob" test load-bearing; if real agents' logprob is poorly calibrated for c (only captures d), schema COULD add beyond it — but the L1 plan explicitly tests this on real benchmarks, which is the right disposition; lexical bag-cosine ≠ neural sentence embedding — stated honestly in ENV CAVEAT and pre-reg, deferred to L1; independence of c and d at rho=0 is a best-case assumption; rho=0.5 was tested and the kill held.]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [None disqualifying — 5 seeds × 12 cells × N=4000, bootstrap B=400 with reported 95% CIs is adequate for the load-bearing deltas; CI<0 in 12/12 cells for vs-difficulty and CI≤0 in 11/12 cells for adds-beyond-logprob is a decisive multi-cell signal, not a fluke; no multiple-comparison correction reported but with effects this consistent and one-sided it doesn't change the verdict; the ONE caveat — high-σ logprob cells where CI straddles 0 — is correctly flagged as artificial-degradation, not a real win.]
RATIONALE: The kill is theoretically over-determined: a noisy single-factor lexical proxy CANNOT dominate (a) a clean readout of the other equally-strong factor d, NOR (b) a joint readout of both (c,d) — this is sufficient-statistic / measurement-error theory, not surprising. The pre-registered anti-circular construction held (oracle gap ~0.2 AUC proves the label isn't leaking through schema tokens), the bootstrap is adequate, the cell-by-cell sign is consistent, and the ENV CAVEAT + L1 plan honestly bound the result to "lexical proxy in synthetic model" and specify the falsifiable L1 redo on real benchmarks. The relabeling diagnosis is correct: schema-geometry adds no incremental signal once you have either a difficulty predictor or the agent's own logprob, and the latter is theoretically guaranteed to integrate confusability anyway. Clean L0 negative, pre-committed kill conditions met, honestly reported — exactly the disposition the hostile committee should reward.
